\subsection{IMU lever-arm installation}
\label{sec:imu-lever-arm-study}
The eight CG-reference records are replayed with \SIlist{10;20;30}{cm} offsets
along body forward, port, and up axes. The installation adds
\begin{equation}
  a_{\mathrm{IMU}}
  = a_{\mathrm{CG}}
  + \dot{\omega}\times r
  + \omega\times(\omega\times r),
  \label{eq:imu-lever-arm}
\end{equation}
to acceleration truth before sensor corruption, leaving CG motion and all
other inputs unchanged. Three matched arms then either retain this term
(unmodeled), remove it using exact angular kinematics (exact-model oracle bound), or estimate
it from corrupted gyroscope data (gyro-model). The latter uses a two-pole
\SI{15}{Hz} low-pass and causal second-order backward difference.
Compensation is applied after sensor corruption, immediately before fusion.
This external compensation experiment is distinct from the optional internal
MEKF lever-arm Jacobian in Sec.~\ref{sec:measurement_model}.

