\IfFileExists{ou3_lever_arm_cutoff.svg}{%
\begin{figure}[t]\centering
\includesvg[width=\columnwidth,inkscapelatex=false]{ou3_lever_arm_cutoff}
\caption{Derivative-band sweep for the 30 cm port arm. Narrow-band phase lag and wide-band differentiated noise compete. The deployed 15 Hz point remains close to the best measured 3-D score; it is not refitted.}\label{fig:imu-lever-arm-cutoff}
\end{figure}
}{}
An installed rotational term can partly cancel an existing estimator residual,
so a smaller pooled error is not evidence for an incorrect sensor location.
The oracle recovers the CG baseline; the gyro model leaves differentiated
noise and lag. These prescribed offsets do not replace a surveyed physical
installation test.
